 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "Ear and Ease, as if the couch were heaven,\nCall me of earth to welcome my coming;\nAnd from that foreign coxcomb's undying fun\nMy exile shall put on a country.\nThen bring me back again thy nation,\nFor ye have not her; they are contented here,\nTheir dear children; only there's danger,\nAnd, no better with them than being.\nIt will be better with you still alive\nThan half my life in Spain: for the nation,\nTo which I owe the present exile,\nWill look o'er her own proud sons' degradation,",
